<% content_for :title, "Getting started · Inkwll" %>

<article class="guide">
  <h1 class="page-title">Getting started</h1>
  <p class="guide__intro text">
    <%= game_name %> is a roleplaying game you play in your browser. You write
    your character's part in stories with other players, in places you can
    walk between.
  </p>

  <section class="guide__section guide__section--first-steps">
    <h2 class="section-title">Your first steps</h2>
    <ol class="guide__steps list">
      <li class="guide__step list__item"><strong class="emphasis">Sign up</strong> for a player account. Your player name is for you; your characters get their own names.</li>
      <li class="guide__step list__item">Go to <strong class="emphasis">My characters</strong> and make a character. Fill in their profile and send them in for staff to approve.</li>
      <li class="guide__step list__item">Once they're approved, pick them in <strong class="emphasis">Playing as</strong> at the top of the page.</li>
      <li class="guide__step list__item">On the front page, press <strong class="emphasis">Enter</strong> on an <%= term(:area).downcase %> to step into the world, then follow the <%= term(:exit, count: 2).downcase %> to look around.</li>
      <li class="guide__step list__item">Find a <%= term(:room).downcase %> you like and start a <%= term(:scene).downcase %>, or join one that's already open there.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <h2 class="guide__heading section-title">How it works</h2>

  <section class="guide__section guide__section--places">
    <h2 class="subsection-title">Getting around</h2>
    <p class="text">
      The world is split into <strong class="emphasis"><%= term(:area, count: 2) %></strong>,
      such as a town or a district. Each <%= term(:area).downcase %> holds
      <strong class="emphasis"><%= term(:room, count: 2) %></strong>: the
      individual spots your character can stand in, like a street, a shop or a flat.
    </p>
    <p class="text">
      <%= term(:room, count: 2) %> are joined by
      <strong class="emphasis"><%= term(:exit, count: 2) %></strong>. Follow a
      <%= term(:exit).downcase %> to walk your character to the next
      <%= term(:room).downcase %>. To start, press <strong class="emphasis">Enter</strong>
      on an <%= term(:area).downcase %> on the front page.
      <%= link_to "Where", where_path %> shows where everyone is.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="guide__section guide__section--scenes">
    <h2 class="subsection-title">Playing a story</h2>
    <p class="text">
      A story is a <strong class="emphasis"><%= term(:scene) %></strong>. Any
      <%= term(:room).downcase %> can hold several <%= term(:scene, count: 2).downcase %>
      at once, so you never have to wait for a quiet spot. Start one, or join
      an open one you find there.
    </p>
    <p class="text">
      Each post you write in a <%= term(:scene).downcase %> is a
      <strong class="emphasis"><%= term(:pose) %></strong>. Most
      <%= term(:scene, count: 2).downcase %> take turns, and the page tells you
      when it's yours. Your open <%= term(:scene, count: 2).downcase %> sit in
      tabs along the top, so you can play more than one at a time.
    </p>
    <p class="text">
      When a <%= term(:scene).downcase %> finishes, it becomes a
      <strong class="emphasis"><%= term(:log) %></strong> and goes into the
      <%= link_to term(:logs_collection), archives_path %> to be read again later.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="guide__section guide__section--from-mush">
    <h2 class="subsection-title">If you're coming from a MUSH</h2>
    <p class="text">
      You'll feel at home. You move a character through <%= term(:room, count: 2).downcase %>
      and <%= term(:exit, count: 2).downcase %>, and play out stories by posing,
      just like on a MUSH. The difference is that it all happens in your browser:
      there's nothing to connect to, and nobody needs a client or a command line.
    </p>
    <h3 class="guide__subheading">What's the same</h3>
    <ul class="list guide__list">
      <li class="list__item">A world you walk around, made of linked <%= term(:room, count: 2).downcase %>.</li>
      <li class="list__item">Characters with profiles, a roster, and staff who approve them.</li>
      <li class="list__item">Stories where each player poses their own character, often taking turns.</li>
      <li class="list__item">Finished stories kept as logs you can read later.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="guide__subheading">What's different</h3>
    <ul class="list guide__list">
      <li class="list__item">A <%= term(:room).downcase %> can hold many <%= term(:scene, count: 2).downcase %> at once, so a busy spot never drowns out a quiet one.</li>
      <li class="list__item">You can play several <%= term(:scene, count: 2).downcase %> at the same time, in tabs, and the page tells you when it's your turn.</li>
      <li class="list__item">There are no commands to type. You write in a box and press a button, and everything else is a link or a menu.</li>
      <li class="list__item">You aren't logged on and "idle". Your game is waiting for you whenever you come back, and alerts tell you when something happens.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="guide__subheading">Words you know, and what we call them</h3>
    <dl class="guide__terms details-list">
      <dt class="details-list__term">Room</dt><dd class="details-list__value"><%= term(:room) %></dd>
      <dt class="details-list__term">Exit</dt><dd class="details-list__value"><%= term(:exit) %></dd>
      <dt class="details-list__term">Scene</dt><dd class="details-list__value"><%= term(:scene) %></dd>
      <dt class="details-list__term">Pose</dt><dd class="details-list__value"><%= term(:pose) %></dd>
      <dt class="details-list__term">Scene log</dt><dd class="details-list__value"><%= term(:log) %>, in the <%= term(:logs_collection) %></dd>
      <dt class="details-list__term">@mail</dt><dd class="details-list__value">Messages</dd>
      <dt class="details-list__term">OOC channel</dt><dd class="details-list__value">OOC Chat</dd>
    </dl>
    <p class="text">
      We write in the <strong class="emphasis">present tense</strong>, the way
      you would on a MUSH: "Lucia pushes open the door and looks around," not
      "Lucia pushed open the door."
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="guide__section guide__section--from-forum">
    <h2 class="subsection-title">If you're coming from a forum</h2>
    <p class="text">
      Writing a reply to someone else's post, then waiting for the next one, will
      feel familiar. You can take your time, and nobody has to be online at once.
      What's different is that the game is also a place: your character stands
      somewhere, and the story happens there.
    </p>
    <h3 class="guide__subheading">What's the same</h3>
    <ul class="list guide__list">
      <li class="list__item">You write a post at your own pace and the others answer when they can.</li>
      <li class="list__item">Stories are kept, in full, to read again.</li>
      <li class="list__item">There are boards for news and wanted ads, much like a forum's sections.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="guide__subheading">What's different</h3>
    <ul class="list guide__list">
      <li class="list__item">Your character moves from <%= term(:room).downcase %> to <%= term(:room).downcase %>, so you find stories by walking around, as well as by browsing.</li>
      <li class="list__item">Everyone in a <%= term(:scene).downcase %> is a character in it, and each <%= term(:pose).downcase %> is written as that character.</li>
      <li class="list__item">Most <%= term(:scene, count: 2).downcase %> take turns, and the page shows whose turn it is.</li>
      <li class="list__item">A <%= term(:scene).downcase %> can be live, with several people posting within minutes, as well as slow.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="guide__subheading">Words you know, and what we call them</h3>
    <dl class="guide__terms details-list">
      <dt class="details-list__term">Thread or topic</dt><dd class="details-list__value"><%= term(:scene) %></dd>
      <dt class="details-list__term">Post</dt><dd class="details-list__value"><%= term(:pose) %></dd>
      <dt class="details-list__term">Forum section</dt><dd class="details-list__value"><%= term(:room) %> (and <%= term(:area).downcase %> for a group of them)</dd>
      <dt class="details-list__term">Private message</dt><dd class="details-list__value">Messages</dd>
      <dt class="details-list__term">Archived thread</dt><dd class="details-list__value"><%= term(:log) %>, in the <%= term(:logs_collection) %></dd>
    </dl>
    <p class="text">
      One habit to change: we write in the <strong class="emphasis">present tense</strong>,
      like a MUSH, not the past tense many forums use. Write "Lucia pushes open the door
      and looks around," not "Lucia pushed open the door."
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="guide__section guide__section--characters">
    <h2 class="subsection-title">Your characters</h2>
    <p class="text">
      You can have more than one character, and switch between them with
      <strong class="emphasis">Playing as</strong>. The
      <%= link_to "Roster", roster_path %> lists characters waiting for a new player.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="guide__section guide__section--talking">
    <h2 class="subsection-title">Talking out of character</h2>
    <p class="text">
      <strong class="emphasis">Messages</strong> are private notes between
      players, outside the story. <strong class="emphasis">OOC Chat</strong> is
      the open chat for everyone, and the
      <%= link_to term(:forum_board, count: 2), forum_boards_path %> hold news
      and wanted ads.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="guide__section guide__section--staff">
    <h2 class="subsection-title">Getting help</h2>
    <p class="text">
      Staff look after the game. If something in a <%= term(:scene).downcase %>
      worries you, use its <strong class="emphasis">Report</strong> link and staff
      will take a look. Everything else lives in the
      <strong class="emphasis">Menu</strong> at the top.
    </p>
  </section>

  <% unless current_account %>
    <p class="guide__join">
      <%= link_to "Sign up", new_registration_path, class: "button" %>
      <%= link_to "Have a look around", root_path, class: "button button--quiet" %>
    </p>
  <% end %>
</article>
